=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-08b63179-28da-5781-a56a-19cfea55072a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-08b63179-28da-5781-a56a-19cfea55072a" :answer-field/id #uuid "08b63179-28da-5781-a56a-19cfea55072a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e0fa109-40a5-55a1-a241-29a6e4d80bf6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98059165-843e-5163-a0dc-8950574baeac" "answer-2eda800c-a21d-570a-852b-6e5077b553c3" "answer-18f71e53-c48d-56dc-a20a-a4556c068cbf" "answer-9e0fa109-40a5-55a1-a241-29a6e4d80bf6" "answer-27af2033-5338-514c-8e18-34428ecb9d3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98059165-843e-5163-a0dc-8950574baeac" :answer/id #uuid "98059165-843e-5163-a0dc-8950574baeac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2eda800c-a21d-570a-852b-6e5077b553c3" :answer/id #uuid "2eda800c-a21d-570a-852b-6e5077b553c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18f71e53-c48d-56dc-a20a-a4556c068cbf" :answer/id #uuid "18f71e53-c48d-56dc-a20a-a4556c068cbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e0fa109-40a5-55a1-a241-29a6e4d80bf6" :answer/id #uuid "9e0fa109-40a5-55a1-a241-29a6e4d80bf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27af2033-5338-514c-8e18-34428ecb9d3c" :answer/id #uuid "27af2033-5338-514c-8e18-34428ecb9d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7198fc6e-53bf-58ce-9c21-b096160c3a27" :question/id #uuid "7198fc6e-53bf-58ce-9c21-b096160c3a27" :question/math-academy-id "q-106550" :question/problem "![](images/9f/9fd54a6b5f5c5c4a711dbdc7de7fcea84177454d6f4a04a1fd647e6a9d93b904.png)\n\nFind the value of $k$ for the parabola $y=-3{x}^{2}+kx+5,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since the graph tells us that the axis of symmetry is $x=-1,$ we will set our result equal to $-1.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=-3$ and $b=k$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{k}{2(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{(-6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-1,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{6} & =-1 \\\\ k & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5bdc9abc-9fd1-5916-ba55-1902c71afb99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5bdc9abc-9fd1-5916-ba55-1902c71afb99" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bdc9abc-9fd1-5916-ba55-1902c71afb99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-06f09f49-4c97-528f-b8de-3a1879e200e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74a39713-92e5-576b-b789-33314d80ed36" "answer-176dee66-a05c-595a-9ab2-46aeebf6b277" "answer-06f09f49-4c97-528f-b8de-3a1879e200e8" "answer-428b9f8a-7e89-5114-a895-5026faee9650" "answer-09fcecc3-19a8-57de-9b01-ad29d32f9d14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74a39713-92e5-576b-b789-33314d80ed36" :answer/id #uuid "74a39713-92e5-576b-b789-33314d80ed36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-176dee66-a05c-595a-9ab2-46aeebf6b277" :answer/id #uuid "176dee66-a05c-595a-9ab2-46aeebf6b277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06f09f49-4c97-528f-b8de-3a1879e200e8" :answer/id #uuid "06f09f49-4c97-528f-b8de-3a1879e200e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-428b9f8a-7e89-5114-a895-5